dict(market='us',ticker='OPTU',slug='chapter11-filing-by-jun27',method='flags-judgment',p=0.65,base=0.55,resolve_by='2027-06-30',
 event='Optimum Communications (ex-Altice USA) or its subsidiary CSC Holdings files for Chapter 11 by 30-Jun-2027',
 evidence="8-K (16-Nov-2026): CSC Holdings 'elected not to make' ~$102.5m of interest due 16-Nov-2026 on its 11.25% 2028, 4.5% 2031 guaranteed and 5% 2031 notes, entering a 30-day grace period; negotiating with 'the steering committee of an ad hoc group of debtholders' that 'holds the vast majority of the nearly $22 billion of debt'; any deal 'would result in a material reduction of the indebtedness'; 'cannot provide any assurances that such an agreement will be reached within the Grace Period or at all'; cash $1.1bn at 30-Sep-2026. 10-Q (Q2 2026, as restated): going-concern 'substantial doubt' with $4.1225bn principal maturing April 2027 and $2.225bn later in 2027 vs cash $1.30bn; Q2 2026 financials restated for an ASC 740 deferred-tax error (non-reliance), alongside cable-franchise impairments.",
 why="Flags-judgment: here the flags (going-concern doubt, skipped coupon, restatement, a $4.1bn April-2027 maturity it cannot pay from cash) all point at the same event and have teeth. With a 'vast majority' ad hoc group already organised, the efficient route to bind holdouts across a ~$22bn multi-tranche structure is usually a pre-packaged or pre-negotiated Chapter 11; an out-of-court exchange is possible but needs near-unanimity. We lean above the reference class.",
 base_reasoning="Reference class (unverified, from memory of rating-agency default studies): issuers that skip a coupon and enter a grace period while negotiating with an ad hoc group end in a bankruptcy filing within ~6–8 months a bit over half the time; the rest are distressed exchanges or extensions.",
 rule="YES if Optimum Communications, Inc., CSC Holdings LLC or any parent/intermediate holding company of CSC Holdings files a voluntary or involuntary petition under Chapter 11 (including a pre-packaged case) on or before 30-Jun-2027, per an 8-K or the bankruptcy docket. A purely out-of-court exchange does not count.",
 source="SEC EDGAR 8-K filings of Optimum Communications (CIK 1702780) / PACER or claims-agent docket",
 sources=[E+'1702780/000170278026000077/optu-20261116.htm','https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=1702780'],tags=['sector-cable','sector-telecom','levered','going-concern','distress'],confidence='verified'),
